<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Saint Lucia Labour Party</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1950">1950</a>–</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Saint Lucia Labour Party is a social-democratic political party in Saint Lucia, founded in 1950 out of the trade union movement. It has alternated in power with the United Workers Party, governing from 1979 to 1982, under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kenny-anthony">Kenny Anthony</a> from 1997 to 2006 and from 2011 to 2016, and under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philip-j-pierre">Philip J. Pierre</a> from 2021.</p></div>
